Biggest argument against altar creation: nobody can agree as to who
it should help.

For helping the weak(ish) characters, having your Quest leader give
you a scroll of altar creation if you're insufficiently advanced seems
like a good idea. To me. At this time.

To make it less certain, have the scroll /try/ to make an altar; a
blessed scroll would have a very good chance of making a coaligned
altar; a cursed scroll would have a very good chance of making a
cross-aligned altar (and converting you) and a small chance of making
a coaligned altar.

Or for more control, b/u/c determines altar type: blessed=lawful, 
uncursed=neutral, cursed=chaotic?

Writing the scroll should take 50+ charges from a magic marker. Wishing
for the scroll would have the same sort of chances as wishing for an
artifact -- you might get a blank or random scroll if it fails.

KPD's idea of letting you _choose_ the deity (and immediately converting)
when you make an altar to is another way to make the process dangerous.

